    if (CollectionUtils.isEmpty(potentialMatches) \u003d\u003d false) {\n+                    message \u003d UnresolvedAttribute.errorMessage(tableName, potentialMatches).replace(\"column\", \"table\");\n+                }\n+                tableNameExpression \u003d new UnresolvedAttribute(tableNameExpression.source(), tableName, null, message);\n+            }\n+            // wrap the table in a local relationship for idiomatic field resolution\n+            else {\n+                localRelation \u003d tableMapAsRelation(source, tables.get(tableName));\n+                // postpone the resolution for ResolveRefs\n+            }\n+\n+            return new Lookup(source, lookup.child(), tableNameExpression, lookup.matchFields(), localRelation);\n+        }\n+\n+        private LocalRelation tableMapAsRelation(Source source, Map\u003cString, Column\u003e mapTable) {","submitted_line":351},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"In the `ResolveLookup` class, the `rule` method converts `tableNameExpression` to a string using `toString()`, which might not be appropriate if `tableNameExpression` is not a literal. Consider using a more robust way to extract the table name.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java--15895:18384","promptId":"#JFC4A","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":15895,"endPos":18384,"startLine":322,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":368,"endLineOffset":5,"length":2490}]}]}]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":341,"start_side":"RIGHT","start_line":338,"line":351,"comment_lines":["[][338]","[][339]","[][340]","[][341]","[][342]","[][343]","[][344]","[][345]","[][346]","[][347]","[][348]","[][349]","[][350]","[][351]"],"review_